---
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { href } from '../lib/site'

const full = `
import { defineCharpente } from 'charpente'

export default defineCharpente({
  defaultTheme: 'solid',
  timeZone: 'Europe/Paris',
  schedule: [{ theme: 'christmas', from: '12-15', to: '12-31' }],
  motion: ['pulse', 'shimmer'],
  timing: { delay: 120, stagger: 40 },
  colorScheme: {
    dark: '[data-theme="dark"]',
    tokens: {
      light: { base: '#e5e7eb' },
      dark: { base: '#2a2d34' },
    },
  },
  themes: {
    brume: {
      extends: 'solid',
      tokens: { base: 'rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.28)' },
      paint: {
        media: { style: { borderRadius: '50%' } },
      },
    },
  },
  motions: {
    rebond: {
      duration: '1.2s',
      staggered: true,
      keyframes: {
        '0%, 100%': { transform: 'translateY(0)' },
        '50%': { transform: 'translateY(-3px)' },
      },
    },
  },
})`

const paintExample = `
themes: {
  stripes: {
    extends: 'solid',
    paint: {
      text: {
        fill: 'repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--charpente-base) 0 0.8lh, transparent 0.8lh 1lh)',
        style: { borderRadius: '2px' },
      },
      media: {
        fill: 'radial-gradient(circle, var(--charpente-strong) 1.4px, transparent 2px), linear-gradient(var(--charpente-base), var(--charpente-base))',
        size: '8px 8px, auto',
      },
    },
  },
}`

const motionExample = `
motions: {
  blink: {
    duration: '900ms',
    easing: 'steps(2, end)',
    iterations: 'infinite',
    keyframes: {
      from: { opacity: '1' },
      to: { opacity: '0.4' },
    },
  },
}`

const schemeExample = `
colorScheme: {
  dark: '[data-theme="dark"]',
  tokens: { dark: { base: '#1f2937', strong: '#374151' } },
}`
---

<Base
  title="Configuration"
  description="Full reference for charpente.config.ts: defaultTheme, schedule, timeZone, motion, timing, colorScheme, themes, motions, tokens and paints."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Configuration</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Everything is set in <code>charpente.config.ts</code>. <code>defineCharpente</code> only
      types the object.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock title="charpente.config.ts" code={full} />

    <h2 id="options">Top-level options</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ref">
        <caption>CharpenteConfig</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Role</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>defaultTheme</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>'solid'</code></td><td>Theme of areas without <code>data-charpente-theme</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>schedule</code></td><td>ScheduleEntry[]</td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Seasonal slots, see <a href={href('calendar')}>the calendar</a>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>timeZone</code></td><td>string (IANA)</td><td>runtime time zone</td><td>Time zone used to read today's date in <code>schedule</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>motion</code></td><td>string or string[]</td><td><code>'shimmer'</code></td><td>Default motion(s). <code>'none'</code> disables.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>timing</code></td><td>Timing</td><td><code>{'{ delay: 120, stagger: 0 }'}</code></td><td>Default delay and offset.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>colorScheme</code></td><td>ColorScheme</td><td>system media query</td><td>Dark mode and per-mode tokens.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>themes</code></td><td>Record&lt;string, ThemeDef&gt;</td><td><code>{'{}'}</code></td><td>Adds themes, or replaces a built-in theme of the same name.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>motions</code></td><td>Record&lt;string, MotionDef&gt;</td><td><code>{'{}'}</code></td><td>Adds motions, or replaces a built-in motion.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 id="timing">timing</h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ref">
        <caption>Timing</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Role</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>delay</code></td><td><code>120</code> ms</td><td>Wait before the skeleton appears. Overridable with <code>--charpente-delay</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>stagger</code></td><td><code>0</code> ms</td><td>Delay added per rank among siblings. Overridable with <code>--charpente-stagger</code>.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 id="colorscheme">colorScheme</h3>
    <p>
      Without <code>dark</code>, dark tokens apply through
      <code>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)</code>. With <code>dark</code>, they apply to
      the element matching the selector, for example the <code>html</code> element carrying
      <code>data-theme="dark"</code>.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock code={schemeExample} />
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ref">
        <caption>ColorScheme</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Role</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>dark</code></td><td>CSS selector</td><td>Replaces the media query with a selector.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>tokens.light</code></td><td>Tokens</td><td>Overrides light-mode tokens, set on <code>:root</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>tokens.dark</code></td><td>Tokens</td><td>Overrides dark-mode tokens.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="themes">Themes</h2>
    <p>
      A theme has three fields, all optional: <code>extends</code>, <code>tokens</code> and
      <code>paint</code>. With <code>extends</code>, the theme inherits the parent's tokens and
      paints: tokens are merged, paints are merged type by type, and within
      <code>style</code> key by key. <code>fill</code> and <code>size</code> replace the
      parent's.
    </p>

    <h3 id="tokens">Tokens</h3>
    <p>
      <code>--charpente-*</code> CSS variables usable in <code>fill</code> and
      <code>style</code>. A token defined in a theme applies to areas of that theme, whether the
      mode is light or dark.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ref">
        <caption>Tokens</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th><th scope="col">Usage</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>base</code></td><td><code>#e5e7eb</code></td><td><code>#2a2d34</code></td><td>Main color of the skeleton.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>strong</code></td><td><code>#c4c8d0</code></td><td><code>#454a55</code></td><td>Outlines, patterns, subtle accents.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>shine</code></td><td><code>rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7)</code></td><td><code>rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)</code></td><td>Glint color of <code>shimmer</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>accent</code></td><td><code>#0891b2</code></td><td><code>#22d3ee</code></td><td>First decoration color.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>accent2</code></td><td><code>#c026d3</code></td><td><code>#e879f9</code></td><td>Second decoration color.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      A <code>--charpente-radius</code> variable (<code>0.35em</code>) is also set on
      <code>:root</code>, used by <code>solid</code> for its corners.
    </p>

    <h3 id="paint">Paint per leaf type</h3>
    <p>
      A "leaf" is an element that is painted as a single piece. <code>paint</code> assigns a
      paint to each of the four types:
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ref">
        <caption>Leaf types</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Elements concerned</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>text</code></td><td>Any element without child elements (a paragraph, a heading, a link, a cell), except media and controls.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>media</code></td><td><code>img</code>, <code>svg</code>, <code>video</code>, <code>canvas</code>, <code>picture</code>, <code>iframe</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>control</code></td><td><code>button</code>, <code>input</code>, <code>select</code>, <code>textarea</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>block</code></td><td>Elements marked <code>data-charpente-block</code>: the element is painted as one block and its children are hidden.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ref">
        <caption>Paint</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Role</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>fill</code></td><td>string</td><td>Comma-separated background layers (<code>background-image</code>). Default: a flat <code>var(--charpente-base)</code> fill.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>size</code></td><td>string</td><td>Size of each layer, in the same order (<code>background-size</code>). <code>auto</code> for an unspecified layer.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>style</code></td><td>Record&lt;string, string&gt;</td><td>Added CSS declarations: <code>borderRadius</code>, <code>clipPath</code>, <code>outline</code>, or an <code>--x</code> variable.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <CodeBlock title="Custom paints" code={paintExample} />

    <h2 id="motions">Motions</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ref">
        <caption>MotionDef</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Role</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>duration</code></td><td>required</td><td>Duration of one cycle, for example <code>'1.4s'</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>easing</code></td><td><code>'ease-in-out'</code></td><td>CSS timing function.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>iterations</code></td><td><code>'infinite'</code></td><td>Number of cycles.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>staggered</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>If true, starts after <code>delay + rank × stagger</code>, like <code>wave</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>layer</code></td><td>none</td><td>Background layer overlaid on the leaves, used by <code>shimmer</code> for its glint.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>keyframes</code></td><td>required</td><td>Animation steps: <code>from</code>, <code>to</code> or percentages, each with its declarations.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <CodeBlock title="A custom motion" code={motionExample} />

    <h2 id="erreurs">Configuration errors</h2>
    <p>The compiler fails with an explicit message in these cases:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>an unknown theme in <code>defaultTheme</code>, <code>extends</code> or <code>schedule</code>;</li>
      <li>a theme that extends itself, directly or in a loop;</li>
      <li>an unknown motion in <code>motion</code>;</li>
      <li>a <code>schedule</code> date that is not in <code>MM-DD</code> form;</li>
      <li>an unknown time zone in <code>timeZone</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      It warns, without failing, when two default motions animate the same property: the
      last one wins.
    </p>

    <h2 id="variables">Exposed CSS variables</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ref">
        <caption>Variables to override inline or in CSS</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Variable</th><th scope="col">Role</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>--charpente-delay</code></td><td>Local delay, with unit (<code>200ms</code>).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>--charpente-stagger</code></td><td>Local offset, with unit.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>--charpente-base</code>, <code>-strong</code>, <code>-shine</code>, <code>-accent</code>, <code>-accent2</code></td><td>Tokens, overridable on any element of the area.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>--charpente-radius</code></td><td>Radius of <code>solid</code>.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
